// Vote options [CR#701.38a]: the words a vote offers, "words with no rules meaning that are each
// connected to a different effect" [CR#701.38b]. A card names its options with lowercase common
// words unless they are exact names (`docs/oracle-style-guide.md` §12, "Randomness, dice, coins,
// and voting"), and its text then mentions them: *votes for sickness or psychosis*, *If psychosis
// gets more votes*, *for each numbers vote*. A mentioned word is a name, not a use of the word
// (CGEL, Ch. 5 §8.2, p. 401), so each option is a Name in scope only on the cards that print it.
// Options that are objects or players (*votes for a player*) are ordinary Noun Phrases and are not
// listed, nor is an option that is a card name, in scope everywhere (*Mines of Moria*).
[
    (name: "aid", cards: ["Elrond of the White Council"]),
    (name: "bribery", cards: ["Tivit, Seller of Secrets"]),
    (name: "carnage", cards: ["Coercive Portal"]),
    (name: "chaos", cards: ["Path of the Animist", "Path of the Enigma", "Path of the Ghosthunter", "Path of the Pyromancer", "Path of the Schemer"]),
    (name: "condemnation", cards: ["Magister of Worth"]),
